139:`src/shared/reads.ts` - beside the protocol, never in a plugin-only namespace. Eight names, frozen: `observe.sessions`, `observe.session`, `observe.live`, `quota.snapshot`, `feed.recent`, `crew.counts`, `repos.list`, `update.status`. Task-system P3 (2026-09-09) added three, frozen the same way: `tasks.board` (re-reads on the `fm:tasks` push, never per task event), `tasks.detail` (re-reads on a `task_changed` / `task_event` for its own id and either board push, including presentation-only changes) and `projects.list` - over `fm:tasks:board`, `fm:tasks:detail`, `fm:projects:list` (`src/shared/tasks.ts` carries the shapes, contract 1.2.0). Git integration PR 1.2 (contract 1.28.0) added `forge.changes` over `fm:forges:changes`: the captain's open proposed changes, read with his in-app sign-in, re-read on the `fm:forges` push and every five minutes. The same phase made `feed.recent` a view over the task record: a task's line is authored by the core from its timeline row (`src/core/tasks/taskFeed.ts`), carries `taskKey`, and the activity frame paints the key as a dim mono prefix; only task-less lines still persist through `activity_events`. Each entry maps a name onto a `surface: "core"` channel of `src/shared/ipc.ts`, a strict args schema (a frame chooses a parameter, never composes a query), and an invalidation - an event predicate, a push channel, a push whose payload is the read's own value (`valueFromPush`, task-system P4), or a poll interval. `reads.test.ts` pins the names, that every entry's request parses against its channel, and that nothing account-, auth-, or card-shaped is in it. The one new read channel is `fm:observe:live`: the core now holds a session's in-flight turn (`src/core/observe/liveBuffer.ts`, fed at the `broadcastEvent` seam), so a frame that never sees raw events can render the stream, and an Observe pane opened mid-turn shows it - something the React tab could not do.
