166:`SidePanelBinding` grew a `frame` arm exactly as `SettingsSectionBinding` did: a panel binds a `PanelSource` plus either a React `Body` (Tier 1) or a `FrameTemplate` (Tier 2), and the registry never knows which. `Rail` mounts a Tier-2 panel as `FrameMount` inside `SidePanelChrome`, with the plugin's declared reads as the frame's whole data surface and no actions - a panel is display. The manifest entry's `size` decides the vehicle's layout: a `fill` panel's frame takes the body's height (the feed), a `content` panel's frame follows the document's own height as the bridge reports it, from zero, rounded up to fit the pixel-rounded viewport. Auto-height panel documents leave vertical scrolling to the host from birth, preventing a fractional-height inner scrollbar from narrowing fluid content; fill documents retain their own scrolling policy (`docs/renderer.md`, "Task record and content-panel sizing").
